title Four reds from two roots, and a meter that cannot read an index page
prompt Autonomous loop -- roster cold first, Standfast on reds, next agent-doable lap Lindy-first crux-first, rota row N mod 5, condense ITINERARY and refill Now, send each finished increment
think Lap index from git log --oneline | wc -l = 3419, so the council rota reads row 3419 mod 5 = 4 -- Earth and Mercury, the concrete: the one-clock naming law, Two Rooms, and the marked value. Two Rooms governed the lap directly. A published number belongs in the checkable room only once something binds it, and this lap found two numbers standing there with nothing behind them.
think Opened the roster cold and it answered guards_red=4. Standfast, so the microkernel lap I had scoped -- Microkit's protection-domain vocabulary as a third caravan rung after refusals.rye and objects.rye -- was set down unstarted and the line stopped on the reds.
think Piped the first roster run through tail and lost its head, which cost a second twenty-five-minute run to see all four names. Worth writing down: a roster whose output is truncated is a roster half read.
think Root one, found by reading the commit rather than the symptom. e9582afd36 added a three-line Where this sits block to 110 room READMEs by walking paths. Two of those paths -- spellbook/README.md and biochemistry/README.md -- are mirrors declared in context/document-mirrors.brix, whose own law says never edit a mirror by hand. A third, docs/README.md, carries a **Ceiling:** <=40 lines header and went to 42.
think Repaired the mirrors the way the descriptor asks: wrote the same block into context/SPELLBOOK.md and context/CHEMICAL_FORMULAS.md at the positions the sweep had used, then ran document_mirror_scan.sh write. The scan reads links_unresolved_from_a_home=0, so the block's three relative links are proven to resolve from both homes rather than assumed to.
think For the ceiling I chose unwrapping over raising. The block's text, links, and meaning are unchanged; only its wrapping moved, onto one line matching that page's own header style, and the page holds the 40 it declares. Raising a ceiling to fit new content is what a ceiling exists to refuse.
think Root two came from asking git rather than guessing. tools/fixtures/geode_libraries_scan.sh counted each room's modules with find "$room" -maxdepth 2 -name '*.rye' -type f, which reads the filesystem. The glow room keeps a .cache of 108 generated .rye files that .gitignore:209 excludes, so the page published 238 where the tree keeps 130.
think That root also explains the fourth red. generated_page_freshness was red for the same stale page, so four reds stood on two roots.
think The pre-commit hook could never have caught it. It regenerates the page when a STAGED change adds or deletes a .rye, and an ignored file is never staged, so the hook is structurally blind here rather than merely unlucky.
think Fixed it by replacing the find with a module_count function that pipes the same find through git check-ignore --stdin --non-matching --verbose and counts the :: lines it prints for paths git does not ignore. Swept every room to check the blast radius: exactly one other room has ignored .rye on disk, seed/, which the census already excludes by name.
think Wrote tools/fixtures/geode_libraries_control.sh, which builds real git repositories in a throwaway pen and runs the real scan inside them rather than copying the rule -- REDS %215's lesson applied on the lap after it was learned. Four readings: an ignored module stays out, the same files count when nothing ignores them, a module written this minute counts, and a room holding only ignored modules leaves the index.
think Then proved the control itself bites, which is the half a passing run cannot show. Pointed at a copy carrying the old rule, it refuses three of the four and passes exactly the one that should pass -- the reading where nothing is ignored.
think Noticed the witness count move 105 to 106 and traced it to my own comment: the by-reference rule counts a witness that writes glow/, and my new prose did. Rewrote it as the `glow` room so the number keeps measuring what it means. Correcting a spurious match is not gaming the meter; leaving it would have published a witness count that included a comment.
obs Then the QA card found the third red, and it is a meter fault rather than a document fault. docs/README.md reads D+ 69 with Reach 0. The card strips tables and bullets, correctly, then divides links by whatever prose survives -- and on that page one surviving line carrying 5 links and 10 words sets the whole reading. docs-geode/libraries/README.md, generated and proven GREEN by its own witness this same lap, reads F on 13 words.
obs Measured the class before believing it: of 130 living pages the card reads, 63 carry under 100 words of prose, so half the population has a per-hundred rate extrapolated from under one unit of its own denominator, and 11 score exactly zero -- docs/ZETA.md on 2 words. The door roster's below-B ratchet ceiling of 1 is that artifact and nothing else.
obs Left it open on purpose rather than patching it. The card is ten corrections deep and REDS %213 already ruled that a meter at that depth takes its own round with the control planted both ways, never a fast fix at the end of a long lap. Named on ITINERARY the way %215 named the Region reading, and it is the next round.
obs Being honest about the shape of that finding: it surfaced while grading a page I had just edited, which is exactly when a person is most tempted to blame the ruler. So I measured the whole population first and would have accepted the D+ had the class been small. It is not small.
obs A low grade is not a red, and this is not the low grade -- it is the meter instructing a repair that would make the artifact worse. Adding prose to an index to raise its word count would damage a page whose own closing line asks that these pages stay few.
loom roster cold_guards=57 cold_red=4 hot_guards=57 roots=2
loom geode_index glow_published=238 glow_tracked=130 ignored_cache=108 rooms_changed=1 rooms_unchanged=37
loom control readings=4 old_rule_refused=3 old_rule_passed=1
loom qa_reach pages_read=130 prose_under_100_words=63 reach_zero=11 min_words=2
file tools/fixtures/geode_libraries_scan.sh module_count asks git check-ignore instead of trusting find
file tools/fixtures/geode_libraries_control.sh four readings on real repositories, proven to bite against the old rule
file tools/g/geode_libraries_witness.rish the control runs before the page is trusted
file docs-geode/libraries/README.md regenerated; the glow row reads 130
file context/SPELLBOOK.md the way-home block added to the canonical, so the mirror regenerates rather than drifts
file context/CHEMICAL_FORMULAS.md the same, at the position the sweep had used
file docs/README.md the way-home block set on one line; the page holds the 40 it declares
file construction/REDS.md rows %216 and %217 booked and closed; %215 folded as they carried the pin past its bound
file construction/archive/REDS-a-body-shared-by-copying-rows-215.md the fold, text unchanged since the row carries no relative links
file construction/CHECKPOINTS.md walk-back nib 8fe50f50f2 before the card's Now was condensed
file construction/ITINERARY.md Now refilled with live work; guard count corrected 54 to 57; four prior laps shelved
file construction/archive/20260825-003210_itinerary-landed-laps.md the four shelved rows, link depth moved with them
obs Read qa_report_card_control.sh before proposing a fix, and it ruled out the obvious one. Section 4 proves Reach falls on link density using a planted page of 20 words and 10 links, so a bare under-100-words floor would exempt the control's own probe and quietly delete a reading that works.
obs The better shape, and both failing pages already carry it: they DECLARE what they are. docs/README.md writes **Depth:** routing in its header and docs-geode/libraries/README.md writes **Kind:** crushed index. So the card can read a page's own declaration the way declared_ceiling reads a page's own limit, and grade an index as one -- reporting link density rather than scoring it. Guarded by two conditions rather than one, so the declaration alone is no exit: the page must declare itself an index AND measure as one, under the prose floor. A planted page declaring routing over 3,000 words stays graded, and the control's 20-word probe declares nothing and stays penalized.
obs Naming the trap in that design before building it: a self-declared exemption is a door, and a door beside a wall makes the wall a habit again. The two-condition form is what keeps it a reading rather than an opt-out, and the control has to plant both halves of it.
recommend keep-going the report card is the next round -- teach Reach to read a page's own **Depth:**/**Kind:** declaration alongside the prose floor, teach Truth that a placeholder shape is an illustration rather than a broken link, plant both in qa_report_card_control.sh from both sides, and let the door roster's below-B ceiling of 1 fall to 0 by measurement rather than by edit
